{"type":"sessionUpdate","data":{"sessionId":"session-1","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call","toolCallId":"call-12","title":"@exorcist/submit_diagnosis","kind":"other","rawInput":{"service":"payments","culprit_deploy":"d-149","culprit_sha":"65c0fca31d0df62c4bab40d2d854c81b1044c650","summary":"Deploy d-149 (commit 65c0fca, 'simplify refund lookup') went out at 11:09:22Z. The payments error ratio rose from 0.025 to 0.286 within 35 seconds. The commit removed the guard in refundTerms that returned DEFAULT_TERMS when findRefund returned undefined, so refundTerms now throws a TypeError whenever no refund record exists. Evidence is strong. Only some requests fail, which fits lookups with no refund record.","evidence":[{"kind":"metric","ref":"metric:payments/error_ratio/15m","detail":"Error ratio went from 0.02501 at 11:09:27Z to 0.2857 at 11:09:57Z, right after the deploy."},{"kind":"error","ref":"error:1","detail":"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'windowDays') at refundTerms (refunds.ts:31:31)"},{"kind":"error","ref":"error:3","detail":"Same TypeError at refunds.ts:31:31. All five sampled errors (error:1 to error:5) show the same message and frame."},{"kind":"log","ref":"log:1","detail":"POST /payments/charge returned 500, while neighbouring requests (log:2 to log:5) returned 200. This matches a partial failure."},{"kind":"deploy","ref":"deploy:d-149","detail":"payments deployed from ref scenario/error-spike at 11:09:22Z, sha 65c0fca, about 5 seconds before the metric jump."},{"kind":"commit","ref":"commit:65c0fca31d0df62c4bab40d2d854c81b1044c650","detail":"Diff removes the 'if (!refund) return DEFAULT_TERMS' guard and replaces it with an unsafe cast 'as RefundTerms'."}],"fix_hint":"Roll payments back to main (c0c6a5c, as in d-148), or restore the guard in refundTerms: if findRefund returns undefined, return DEFAULT_TERMS. Drop the 'as RefundTerms' cast."}}}}
